      "value": "2025-11-04",
      "strength": "corroborated",
      "quote": "THE WEAKEST OF THIS SET, and it rests on a bracket rather than a document. No source names the day: the cited clerk page, the city's 2025 elections index and its early-voting notices all print none. A Massachusetts city holds its biennial municipal election on the Tuesday after the first Monday in November of an odd-numbered year, and this corpus publishes North Adams 2021 as 2021-11-02 and 2023 as 2023-11-07 -- both exactly that Tuesday, bracketing 2025 on either side. The first Monday of November 2025 is the 3rd, so the Tuesday is the 4th.",
